---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Preview terms — MojiPond";
const description = "Terms for using pre-release builds of MojiPond.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} noindex>
  <article class="legal-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Preview terms</p>
    <h1>MojiPond is still pre-release software.</h1>
    <div class="legal-note">
      <strong
        >Do not treat a development build as a signed public release.</strong
      >
      <p>Last updated August 1, 2026.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>Using a preview build</h2>
    <p>
      Preview builds exist for testing. Features can change, and some editors
      may behave differently from the controlled test fixtures. Keep a copy of
      any emoji pack you import.
    </p>

    <h2>Your emoji packs</h2>
    <p>
      You are responsible for the artwork and metadata you import. Only use
      files you own or have permission to use. MojiPond does not grant rights to
      third-party emoji packs.
    </p>

    <h2>macOS permissions</h2>
    <p>
      You choose whether to grant Input Monitoring, Accessibility, and optional
      Event Posting. macOS lets you revoke them at any time in System Settings.
      Without the required permissions, global autocomplete will not work.
    </p>

    <h2>No warranty for preview builds</h2>
    <p>
      The preview is provided as available, without a promise that it will work
      in every app or preserve compatibility between builds. Stop using it if it
      interferes with typing or another input tool.
    </p>

    <h2>Public release terms</h2>
    <p>
      These preview terms will be reviewed before the first signed and notarized
      release. The release page will name the applicable license and
      version-specific notices.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
